# r1113 Power Grid boot on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-14.jar (sha1 d80a8babfdc0, port
# phase 9.2: P9b circuit design table, schematic item, editor packets; fixes B20 to B24). One boot, one batch, this order:
#   1. SQ-PWG-72 boot check (version, phase 9.2, registries, menus, packets, 94 recipes, zpwg9 / zpwg9b check, reload)
#   2. SQ-PWG-57 rerun for fix B20 (copy of pwg10b.qb's row; the -10 failure was
#      `held=ae2:wireless_terminal fe 0/3200000 -> 0/3200000 charge 20000/20000 -> 0/20000`)
#   3. P9b rows: SQ-PWG-73, -74, -75 (queue run order; CQ-PWG-24 / -25 are client rows, not here)
# Group A superflat, level pwg14, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks (box selector) and stops mob spawning.
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P9b   X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850 (SQ-PWG-72 forceload, kept; -73 Z 1810 to 1825, -74 / -75 Z 1820 to 1835)
#   P7    X 1095 to 1115, Z 1535 to 1545 (SETUP14P7; SQ-PWG-57's fake player at 1100 -60 1540, no blocks)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-14.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg14 A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-14.jar: remove -13 and
#     older; cc-tweaked-1.19.2-1.101.4.jar present); sha1sum of the jar starts d80a8babfdc0
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe pwg_p8_probe pwg_p9a_probe pwg_p9b_probe; do
#     cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done      (ten probes, the CURRENT copies;
#     p9b has the CircuitSchematicItem class check by instanceof)
#   ponder datapack from the -14 jar (77 structure files; SQ-PWG-72 checks it is enabled, no row places from it):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwg14/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-14.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwg14/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwg14/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   find OUT/srv/pwg14/datapacks/pwgponder -name '*.nbt' | wc -l      (77)
#   Loading Protection (shorter protection window, as pwg10 / pwg12):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Nothing else: no CC program, no other datapack, no config edit (the P9b rows use /give-free probe slots and packets).
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg14.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg14
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: tick waits are sleeps (pace 1 s after each command); SQ-PWG-57 adds its own
# forceload (SETUP14P7) and, for B20, checks only that the held item gains FE and the charge falls (the -10 pattern
# 0 -> 0 with the charge emptied is rejected); the wireless terminal may take the whole 20000 in one tick, so the old
# `1\d{4}` charge bound is dropped (record FE gained = charge lost per tick); SQ-PWG-73's 100 V / 130 V reads use
# 1 s sleeps after the source change.
pace 1

## SQ-PWG-72 | -14 loads (phase 9.2): version, registries (menus 7), packets, 94 recipes, zpwg9 check, zpwg9b check, ponder datapack, reload
bootexpect Power grid starting, prepare to be electrocuted \(1\.19\.2 port, phase 9\.2\)
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect Loaded 28 component items
bootreject InvalidInjectionException|InjectionError|Critical injection failure|Mixin apply failed
bootreject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(/ERROR\]|@Redirect|conflict).*powergrid\.mixins\.json
bootreject Failed to parse component item
> forceload add 1090 1805 1130 1850
sleep 8
> zpwg mods powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg\] done 30
> zpwg ns powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg\] ns powergrid total 30
> zpwg3 recipes powergrid
waitlog \[zpwg3\] recipes \d+ 30
> zpwg9 check
waitlog \[zpwg9\] done 30
> zpwg9b check
waitlog \[zpwg9b\] done 30
> datapack list enabled
sleep 1
shell grep -n -E 'component items|powergrid\.mixins\.json|Mixin apply failed|circuit_design|CircuitDesign' logs/latest.log | head -40
> reload
waitlog Loaded 28 component items 180
sleep 5
> zpwg9b check
sleep 3
shell grep -n -E 'component items|powergrid\.mixins\.json|Mixin apply failed|circuit_design|CircuitDesign' logs/latest.log | tail -20
expect \[zpwg\] mod powergrid 0\.6\.2-ce-19\.2-14
