## SQ-PWG-57 | PWG-34 worn battery: output fraction (0.25 floor, 0 below one use), Capacity max, worn tick moves FE to the held item
> zpwg7 fp 1100 -60 1540
> zpwg7 wear 20000
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 wear 8000
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 wear 2000
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 wear 0
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 wear 20000 2
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 wear 40000 1
> zpwg7 bat
> zpwg7 feitems
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=20000/20000 output=1
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=8000/20000 output=0\.8
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=2000/20000 output=0\.25
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=0/20000 output=0
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=20000/60000 output=0\.667
expect \[zpwg7\] bat charge=40000/40000 output=1
expect \[zpwg7\] feitems [1-9]\d*:
capture FE \[zpwg7\] feitems \d+: (?:.*? )?([a-z0-9_.-]+:[a-z0-9_/.-]+)\(0/[1-9]\d*\)
> zpwg7 hold {FE}
> zpwg7 wear 20000
> zpwg7 worn 1
> zpwg7 worn 20
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg7\] worn x1 held=\S+ fe 0/\d+ -> [1-9]\d*/\d+ charge 20000/20000 -> \d+/20000
reject \[zpwg7\] worn x\d+ held=\S+ fe 0/\d+ -> 0/\d+ charge [1-9]\d*/\d+ -> 0/
expect \[zpwg7\] worn x20 held=
reject \[zpwg7\] worn: no battery worn
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look B20 rerun (-10 failed: held=ae2:wireless_terminal fe 0/3200000 -> 0/3200000 charge 20000/20000 -> 0/20000): FE gained must equal charge lost on the x1 line (all 20000 in one tick is a pass for a big buffer); record the feitems list and the chosen {FE}; record FE gained and charge lost per tick (row: equal; one tick moves at most what the item accepts); capture FAIL = no empty FE item in the pack: then the worn tick is CQ-PWG-18 only

## SQ-PWG-73 | PWG-41 (P9b part): design table power by cord (100 / 130 V), menus, editor packets (fromboard, screen), B21 reach, item NBT round trip, write (B23) and load
> zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1810 powergrid:circuit_design_table facing=north
waitlog \[zpwg3\] done 20
> zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1813 powergrid:socket facing=down
> zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1813 100
> zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1813 0 1100 -60 1813 0
> zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1813 1 1100 -60 1813 1
> zpwg9b cord 1100 -60 1813 1100 -60 1810
sleep 1
> zpwg9b tbe 1100 -60 1810
> zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1813 130
sleep 1
> zpwg9b tbe 1100 -60 1810
> zpwg9b menus 1100 -60 1810
# packets
> zpwg9 board 1106 -60 1810 resistor
waitlog \[zpwg9\] done 20
> zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1812
> zpwg9b fromboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1810 Test Resistor
> zpwg9b itemrt 1100 -60 1810
> zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 1
> zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 2
> zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 0
# reach (B21): 15 blocks away
> zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1825
> zpwg9b fromboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1810 Far Name
> zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 1
> zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1812
# write and load (B23)
> zpwg9b slot 1100 -60 1810 1 create:empty_schematic
> zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810
> zpwg9b slot 1100 -60 1810 1 create:empty_schematic
> zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810
> zpwg9b move 1100 -60 1810 2 0
> zpwg9b load 1100 -60 1810
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg9b\] cord table .* result=true/true
expect \[zpwg9b\] cord entities near: (?!none)
expect \[zpwg9b\] table at 1100 -60 1810 state=.*powered=false.* light=0 isPowered=false power=2[01]\.\d
expect \[zpwg9b\] table at 1100 -60 1810 state=.*powered=true.* light=7 isPowered=true power=3[45]\.\d
expect \[zpwg9b\] menu 0 powergrid:circuit_design_table class=CircuitDesignTableMenu slots=39$
expect \[zpwg9b\] menu 1 powergrid:circuit_design_table_edit .*slots=36$
expect \[zpwg9b\] menu 2 powergrid:circuit_design_table_load .*slots=0$
expect \[zpwg9b\] fromboard packet bytes=[1-9]\d{2,}
expect \[zpwg9b\] fromboard applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table class
expect \[zpwg9b\] fromboard table before: schematic name=null components=0 after: schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3$
expect \[zpwg9b\] itemrt .*Schematic components=3 name="Test Resistor".* safeNbtEqual=true
expect \[zpwg9b\] screen 1 applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table_edit
expect \[zpwg9b\] screen 2 applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table_load
expect \[zpwg9b\] screen 0 applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table class
expect \[zpwg9b\] fromboard table before: schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3 after: schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3$
expect \[zpwg9b\] screen 1 applied menu=inventory
reject \[zpwg9b\] .*"Far Name"
count \[zpwg9b\] slot 2 powergrid:circuit_schematic x1 Schematic components=3 name="Test Resistor"$ == 2
count \[zpwg9b\] slot 1 create:empty_schematic x1$ == 2
expect \[zpwg9b\] slot 0 powergrid:circuit_schematic x1 Schematic components=3 name="Test Resistor"$
expect \[zpwg9b\] table schematic name=null components=0
count \[zpwg9b\] table schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3 >= 1
reject \[zpwg9b\] .*apply threw
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look cord socket line result=true/true (or a cord-next message; record); 100 V power about 20.8, 130 V about 35.2 (480 ohm); first write: slot 1 empty, slot 2 the schematic, table name=null components=0; second write (B23): slot 1 keeps the blank, slot 2 unchanged; load: slot 0 the schematic, slot 1 the blank, table "Test Resistor" components=3; packet sizes a few hundred bytes

## SQ-PWG-74 | PWG-41: a design written on the table becomes a board (creative sneak-use, place) that solves like the source board
> zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810
waitlog \[zpwg9b\] done 20
> zpwg9b toboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1820
> zpwg9 bmap 1106 -60 1820
> zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1826 powergrid:current_gauge facing=north
> zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1823 10
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1823 0 1106 -60 1826 0
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1826 1 1106 -60 1820 0
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1823 1 1106 -60 1820 1
sleep 1
> zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1826
> zpwg9 bcomp 1106 -60 1820
> zpwg9 bmap 1106 -60 1810
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg9b\] slot 1 empty$
expect \[zpwg9b\] slot 2 powergrid:circuit_schematic x1 Schematic components=3
expect \[zpwg9b\] toboard use .* result=SUCCESS -> powergrid:circuit_board x1 Schematic components=3
expect \[zpwg9b\] place .* result=(SUCCESS|CONSUME) -> Block\{powergrid:circuit_board\}
expect \[zpwg9b\] toboard board schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3 terminals=2$
expect \[zpwg9\] board at 1106 -60 1820 .*components=3 terminals=2
count \[zpwg9\] bundle \d+: connector@0,6#0\* resistor@5,6#0$ >= 2
count \[zpwg9\] bundle \d+: connector@11,6#0\* resistor@5,6#1$ >= 2
expect \[zpwg9\] part resistor@5,6 destroyed=false props\[.*resistor_value=100(\.0)?\b
reject \[zpwg9b\] toboard no board entity
reject \[zpwg9\] .*NaN
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look gauge about 0.1 A (10 V / 100 ohm, 2 %; be line); toboard use item has no name (upstream resets it); record the placed board's facing / rotation; both bmaps list the same two bundles (if the gauge reads 0, rewire by bmap and record)

## SQ-PWG-75 | board edit menu (creative only) and board editor save: B22 name kept, survival refused, B21 reach
> zpwg9b fp 1106 -60 1822
waitlog \[zpwg9b\] done 20
> zpwg9b buse 1106 -60 1820
